{"schema_version": 3, "source_hash": "25f91db2495688a6", "candidate": {"id": "cand-010", "name": "Kieran Walsh", "raw_cv": "KIERAN WALSH\nkieran.walsh@email.com | London, UK\n\nSENIOR DATA ENGINEER\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nData engineer with 5 years of experience across e-commerce, media, and fintech sectors. Proficient in Python, dbt, and Snowflake. Strong background in data product development and stakeholder management.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nSenior Data Engineer \u2014 Deliveroo, London (2021\u2013present)\n- Built and maintained dbt models for the rider and restaurant analytics platform\n- Designed Airflow pipelines for daily reporting and product analytics\n- Collaborated with product and finance teams to define key metrics\n- Refactored legacy ETL jobs in Python, reducing runtime by 40%\n\nData Engineer \u2014 The Guardian, London (2019\u20132021)\n- Built audience and content analytics pipelines in BigQuery\n- Worked on subscriber lifetime value modelling data feeds\n\nSKILLS\nPython, SQL, dbt, Snowflake, BigQuery, Airflow, Docker, Git\n\nEDUCATION\nBSc Statistics \u2014 University of Warwick (2016\u20132019)\n\nRIGHT TO WORK\nBritish citizen (Irish dual national)", "raw_linkedin": "Data engineer with five years of experience across some of London's most interesting data-intensive companies \u2014 Deliveroo and The Guardian. I love building data infrastructure that actually gets used and trusted by stakeholders. Strong in dbt, Python, and Snowflake. Interested in my next challenge \u2014 ideally somewhere with interesting data and a healthy work-life balance culture.", "raw_interview_transcript": "Interviewer: Kieran, what draws you to financial data engineering after time in media and e-commerce?\n\nKieran: I'm genuinely attracted to the rigour of financial data. In media you can get away with approximate numbers; in fintech the reconciliation has to be exact. I find that challenge appealing. I've been picking up knowledge on the regulatory side in my own time \u2014 reading about CASS, MiFID data requirements.\n\nInterviewer: Good to hear. What about the five-days-in-office arrangement?\n\nKieran: That's the one thing I'd want to talk through. I'm fully committed to this role and the company, but I've been hoping for a four-day working week. It's been a personal goal for a while \u2014 I coach youth football on Friday evenings and having a compressed schedule would let me manage that much better. Is there any flexibility there, or is five full days genuinely fixed?\n\nInterviewer: It's fixed, unfortunately. The role requires five days at Canary Wharf \u2014 it's a team and culture thing, not just a policy.\n\nKieran: I understand. I'm not going to pretend it's ideal for me. I'd still be very interested in the role \u2014 I'm not going to walk away over it \u2014 but I want to be honest that it's a consideration for me.\n\nInterviewer: We appreciate the honesty. Let's continue the conversation. Salary?\n\nKieran: I'm at \u00a374,000. I'd be looking for \u00a378\u201382,000.", "years_experience": 5.0, "skills": ["Python", "SQL", "dbt", "Snowflake", "BigQuery", "Airflow", "Docker", "Git"], "industries": ["e-commerce", "media", "fintech"], "seniority_level": "senior", "management_experience": false, "education_level": "bachelor", "career_trajectory": "ascending", "interview_score": 0.82, "culture_fit_score": 0.75, "constraints": [{"id": "feebaab9", "type": "hard", "side": "candidate", "category": "compensation", "description": "Current salary \u00a374,000", "canonical_key": "salary_current", "value": 74000.0, "operator": "requires", "weight": 1.0, "confidence": 0.98, "currency": "GBP"}, {"id": "ea99980e", "type": "hard", "side": "candidate", "category": "compensation", "description": "Minimum salary expectation \u00a378,000", "canonical_key": "salary_min", "value": 78000.0, "operator": "min", "weight": 1.0, "confidence": 0.95, "currency": "GBP"}, {"id": "a6885908", "type": "hard", "side": "candidate", "category": "compensation", "description": "Maximum salary expectation \u00a382,000", "canonical_key": "salary_max", "value": 82000.0, "operator": "max", "weight": 1.0, "confidence": 0.93, "currency": "GBP"}, {"id": "e2edd718", "type": "soft", "side": "candidate", "category": "work_arrangement", "description": "Prefers four-day working week; has coaching commitment Friday evenings", "canonical_key": "office_days_per_week", "value": 4.0, "operator": "prefers", "weight": 1.0, "confidence": 0.88, "currency": null}, {"id": "24bf21ab", "type": "hard", "side": "candidate", "category": "location", "description": "Role requires five days at Canary Wharf; five-day requirement is fixed per employer", "canonical_key": "office_location", "value": "Canary Wharf", "operator": "requires", "weight": 1.0, "confidence": 0.85, "currency": null}, {"id": "e852f8df", "type": "soft", "side": "candidate", "category": "values", "description": "Seeks healthy work-life balance culture", "canonical_key": "work_life_balance", "value": "healthy", "operator": "prefers", "weight": 1.0, "confidence": 0.82, "currency": null}, {"id": "5ca710d5", "type": "soft", "side": "candidate", "category": "domain", "description": "Attracted to fintech sector; values rigorous financial data and regulatory knowledge", "canonical_key": "domain_preference", "value": "fintech", "operator": "prefers", "weight": 1.0, "confidence": 0.8, "currency": null}, {"id": "2ac6cdb2", "type": "hard", "side": "candidate", "category": "work_authorization", "description": "British citizen (Irish dual national); right to work in UK confirmed", "canonical_key": "right_to_work", "value": "UK", "operator": "requires", "weight": 1.0, "confidence": 0.99, "currency": null}], "discipline": "data"}, "embedding": [-0.04132080078125, 0.053314208984375, 0.039215087890625, -0.0059356689453125, 0.0244140625, -0.038177490234375, 0.01256561279296875, 0.050262451171875, -0.002094268798828125, 0.0181884765625, -0.00946807861328125, -0.025909423828125, -0.026123046875, -0.0119